meta {
  name: Disconnect GitHub Installation
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

delete {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/github/installation
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

docs {
  # Disconnect GitHub Installation

  Clears `users.github_installation_id` for the current user and best-effort
  revokes the install on GitHub. The revoke is best-effort: failures are
  logged but never block the disconnect (the local link is the source of
  truth for whether we attempt to use the App).

  ## Permissions

  ADMIN or LECTURER.

  ## Returns

  `204 No Content` on success (also when the user had no installation linked).
}
